==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The enemies are stronger here than the previous rounds, so the [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] will most likely not be able to get you through this, unless level 20 or in their [[True Form]]s. What you will need for this is long-range units that can outrange Teacher Bear and powerful [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]] that can take out the Doge Darks quickly, as all enemies are at 150% magnification. Examples of these would be [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]], or if you have him, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. Of course, if you are in late early-game or above, this stage should be a cakewalk with [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]].

